{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-3504","published":"2026-08-30T04:14:21Z","modified":"2026-08-30T04:32:26.919006860Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-19654"],"summary":"rsyslog security update","details":"RSYSLOG is the rocket-fast system for log processing.It offers high-performance, great security features and a modular design. While it started as a regular syslogd, rsyslog has evolved into a kind of swiss army knife of logging, being able to accept inputs from a wide variety of sources, transform them, and output to the results to diverse destinations.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA unauthenticated remote peer may lead rsyslogd to crash due to a flaw in the optional imptcp module. A crafted input sequence during oversize-frame recovery can cause an invalid internal message length and terminate rsyslogd. No confidentiality or integrity impact, privilege escalation, or code execution has been identified. imtcp and the default imptcp framing modes are not affected.(CVE-2026-19654)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"rsyslog","ecosystem":"openEuler:22.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/rsyslog&distro=openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["rsyslog-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","rsyslog-crypto-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","rsyslog-debuginfo-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","rsyslog-debugsource-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","rsyslog-elasticsearch-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","rsyslog-gnutls-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","rsyslog-gssapi-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","rsyslog-hiredis-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","rsyslog-kafka-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","rsyslog-mmaudit-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","rsyslog-mmjsonparse-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","rsyslog-mmkubernetes-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","rsyslog-mmnormalize-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4.aarch64.rpm","rsyslog-mmsnmptrapd-8.2210.0-11.oe2203sp4